cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Mosaic: a research programme in computational cognitive science"
message: >-
  Cite a pinned version, never the repository as it stands. `main` is the
  programme's current state of belief, not its published state, so an
  unversioned citation names a target designed to move — and it moves in the
  way that matters, since a MINOR bump is a Protective Belt rung changing.
  Set `version` to the `research-vX.Y.Z` tag you read, or, for anything
  predating a tag, set `commit` to the sha.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Litov
    given-names: Noah
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-2564-7614"
repository-code: "https://github.com/NGL321/mosaic"
url: "https://github.com/NGL321/mosaic"
abstract: >-
  A long-running, LLM-accelerated research programme investigating cognition
  as a heterogeneous network of inference engines whose schemas each carry
  their own metric space, and the Transport between them — of which the
  primary observable is where Transport fails. Framed on Lakatos: a Hard Core
  that is not revised, a Protective Belt of falsifiable claims that is, and a
  Positive Heuristic governing how belt rungs are added and retired.
keywords:
  - computational cognitive science
  - research programme
  - interpretability
  - open notebook science
# Split by artifact kind, not by track — MIT for code, CC BY 4.0 for the prose
# record. The path table that decides which is which lives in README.md.
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0

